2026-07-28 22:01:26,371 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What safety analyses are planned?", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 14, "section": "Data Analyses"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 68, "section": "9.8.1 General Considerations"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 13, "section": "Data Analyses"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 67, "section": "9.4.4 Safety Analysis Set"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 66, "section": "9 STATISTICAL METHODS"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 29, "section": "3.3 Safety Review Committee"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 15, "section": "Data Analyses"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 16, "section": "Protocol No.: CTJ301UC201"}], "context_char_count": 7931, "response": "## Planned Safety Analyses\n\n### 1. General Approach\nAll statistical analyses will be detailed in a separate **Statistical Analysis Plan (SAP)** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p66). Safety analyses will be **summarized descriptively by treatment groups**, and **no statistical testing for comparison of treatment groups will be performed** for safety variables (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p13; p68).\n\n### 2. Safety Analysis Set\nThe **Safety Analysis Set** will include **all randomised patients who received at least one dose of IMP**, with treatment assignment according to actual treatment received (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p67).\n\n### 3. Safety Parameters Evaluated\nThe following safety data will be assessed (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p68):\n- **Adverse events**\n- **Concomitant medications**\n- **Vital signs**\n- **Clinical laboratory test values**\n- **12-lead ECG**\n\nComplete **data listings and summary tables** will be created for all safety information (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p68).\n\n### 4. Baseline Definition\nFor safety data, **Baseline** is defined as the **last observed value collected prior to the start of treatment** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p68).\n\n### 5. Safety Review Committee (SRC)\nA **Safety Review Committee (SRC)** will be established as an expert advisory group responsible for evaluating **cumulative safety data at regular intervals**. The SRC will:\n- Review **blinded data**\n- Evaluate safety concerns\n- Make recommendations to the Sponsor regarding trial conduct and possible modifications\n\nThe SRC will comprise **at least a medical monitor, a physician, and a pharmacologist**. A SRC Working Procedure will be prepared and signed **prior to enrolment of the first patient** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p29).\n\n### 6. Pharmacokinetics (PK)\nThe PK parameters of TJ301 will be derived using a **noncompartmental method** and summarized using **descriptive statistics** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p13).", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 66, "section": "9 STATISTICAL METHODS", "exactText": "All statistical analyses will be detailed in a separate Statistical Analysis Plan (SAP).", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999997, 715.7039829101564, 477.96, 705.4149752178487]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 13, "section": "Data Analyses", "exactText": "Safety analyses will be summarized descriptively by treatment groups. No statistical testing for comparison of treatment groups will be performed for safety variables. The PK parameters will be derived using noncompartmental method. The PK of TJ301 will be summarized using descriptive statistics.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 372.02398291015623, 531.72, 346.4949752178485]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 68, "section": "9.8.1 General Considerations", "exactText": "Safety parameters will be evaluated for the safety analysis data set. Complete data listings and summary tables will be created for all safety information and include adverse events, concomitant medications, vital signs, clinical laboratory test values, and 12-lead ECG. For safety data, Baseline will be defined as the last observed value collected prior to the start of treatment. No statistical testing for comparison of treatment groups will be performed for safety variables.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 124.58398291015624, 399.6, 114.29497521784856]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 67, "section": "9.4.4 Safety Analysis Set", "exactText": "The Safety analysis set will include all randomised patients who received at least one dose of IMP, with treatment assignment according to actual treatment received.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 721.7039829101564, 549.12, 696.2949752178487]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 29, "section": "3.3 Safety Review Committee", "exactText": "A Safety Review committee (SRC) will be established. The SRC is an expert advisory group commissioned and charged with the responsibility of evaluating, primarily, cumulative safety data at regular intervals. The SRC will review blinded data and provide recommendations to the Sponsor based on their evaluation.", "bboxes": [[72.0, 579.2639829101564, 555.24, 523.3749752178487]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": false, "chunks_compressed": true, "embedding_ms": 354.7829999879468, "embedding_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_search_ms": 1756.4060830045491, "retrieval": {"chunk_cache_hit": false, "hybrid_search": true, "cache_hit": true, "embedding_ms": 0.0, "db_search_ms": 596.3619579852093, "hybrid_parallel_ms": 992.6258329942357, "vector_count": 20, "bm25_count": 0, "fused_count": 19, "retrieval_total_ms": 993.0676670046523}, "original_chunk_count": 19, "compression_ms": 0.37291698390617967, "compressed_chunk_count": 8, "llm_call_ms": 15304.133375000674, "generation_total_ms": 19039.37145799864}}
2026-07-28 22:02:55,456 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "What fields should be included in the eCRF?", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 73, "section": "11.3 Confidentiality of Patient Data"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 58, "section": "8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.1 Recruitment"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 38, "section": "4.4 Withdrawal Criteria"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 80, "section": "16.1 Investigator File"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 37, "section": "4.3.1 Prior and Concomitant Therapies"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 70, "section": "Trial-specific Source Data Requirements"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 75, "section": "12.2 Deviations from the Protocol"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 52, "section": "6.4 Unscheduled Visits"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 78, "section": "14.5 Patient Information and Consent"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 76, "section": "13.1 Clinical Trial Report"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 64, "section": "Expedited Reporting by the Sponsor or CRO"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 29, "section": "3.3 Safety Review Committee"}], "context_char_count": 17302, "response": "## Fields to be Included in the eCRF\n\nBased on the protocol, the following fields and data categories should be documented in the electronic Case Record Form (eCRF):\n\n### 1. Patient Identification & Screening\n- Unique **screening number** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p36)\n- **Reason for screening failure**, if applicable (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p36)\n- Selected data for all screened patients (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p36)\n\n### 2. Adverse Event Log\nEach adverse event entry must include (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p58):\n- Adverse event description\n- Date of onset (time, if applicable)\n- Intensity\n- Causal relationship to IMP\n- Action taken to IMP\n- Other action taken\n- Date and time of outcome\n- Outcome\n- Seriousness\n\n### 3. Serious Adverse Events (SAEs)\n- **Demographics**, **Adverse Event Log**, **Medical History Log**, and **Concomitant Medication Log** are mandatory for initial and follow-up SAE reports (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p63)\n\n### 4. Concomitant Medications\n- Details of all **concomitant medications** and the **main reason for prescription** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p37)\n- Prior treatment for UC within 12 months of Visit 1 (Screening) (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p37)\n\n### 5. Withdrawal / Discontinuation\n- **Date of premature termination** and **main reason for discontinuation** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p38)\n- Patient status must be **registered as discontinued** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p38)\n- If the reason for discontinuation is an adverse event, the specific event must be recorded (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p38)\n\n### 6. Unscheduled Visits\n- Description and **reason for unscheduled visits**, including any additional assessments or laboratory samples (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p52)\n\n### 7. Protocol Deviations\n- Any **protocol deviation**, including description, relevant dates (start and stop), and action taken (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p75)\n\n### 8. General Notes\n- Patients are identified by an **assigned identification number only** \u2014 not by name \u2014 in the eCRF (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p73)\n- All entries must be made **timely** after a visit or when data become available, and must be **approved/authorised by the Investigator** via electronic signature (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p71)\n- Any corrections are tracked automatically via **audit trail** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p71)", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 71, "section": "10.2 Electronic Case Record Form", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 428.42398291015644, 554.4000000000001, 387.7749752178487], [71.99999999999994, 183.1439829101563, 551.0399999999998, 142.4949752178486], [71.99999999999994, 711.8639829101563, 550.92, 671.2149752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 63, "section": "8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 135.8639829101562, 541.0800000000002, 110.45497521784853], [72.0, 369.2639829101563, 555.6, 267.89497521784847]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 73, "section": "11.3 Confidentiality of Patient Data", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.0, 174.5039829101563, 549.8400000000001, 118.73497521784861], [71.99999999999983, 421.46398291015635, 540.8399999999997, 380.8149752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 58, "section": "8.2.2 Recording of Adverse Events", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000011, 188.78398291015662, 511.32, 163.25497521784894]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.1 Recruitment", "exactText": "", "bboxes": [[72.00000000000006, 453.62398291015614, 336.24000000000007, 443.3349752178484]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 38, "section"